  "id": "DrugBank_DB14568 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ivosidenib may be associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23) through a pathway involving Glasdegib. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, each indicating a potential therapeutic or pathophysiological link. Ivosidenib is linked to Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia and Glasdegib, which in turn is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23). Similarly, Ivosidenib is also connected to Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome, which also links to Glasdegib and the same leukemia subtype. These findings suggest that Ivosidenib may act as a potential therapeutic agent or modulator in this specific subtype of acute myeloid leukemia. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating a possible role in the pathogenesis or treatment of this condition. However, the exact mechanism of action and the extent of Ivosidenib's efficacy in this context remain to be fully elucidated.",
